                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I don't dislike the game but I can't bring myself to recommend it to the steam community.\n\nI learned of the game through a story on NPR - a group/class project at a local University in my area.  I'm also always looking for good local-coop games to play together with my two boys.\n\nTechnically, the game is flawless.  Smooth fast graphics, highly responsive, no lag, great sound and pretty pictures.   Also, I've always enjoyed rogue-like games and this was a nice twist.\n\nUnfortunately, that's about it in terms of gameplay.  Not to be crass, but it feels like a school group project - a roguelike game made by committee that's a mile wide and an inch deep.  Like any game, once the pretty pictures wear off, there needs to be something of substance behind it.  Even the original nethack games had a leveling system - and with good reason!  You need some reason to keep playing and go for just one more dungeon.   More than 4 monsters and a few bosses would be a good start. \n\nI guess it's easier to give a school grade for solid graphics and technical savvy then it is to judge depth or playability.  And having the goal of publishing to Steam is a good carrot to motivate students to meet a deadline I suppose. \n\nMy boys (8 & 10 yo) had fun with the novelty of the game for about 15 minutes.  But once they realized that there was only more of the same around each corner, they lost interest quick - and so did I.",
